{% comment %}
  Where and when management happened: years across, place along the island up (Cape Point at the bottom, north up).
  Fills, road moves, bridges and the Buxton groins from timeline.json (tools/hatteras_timeline_data.py), with the named
  storms along the top; each mark links to its Management sub-page. Script: assets/hatteras/js/management-map.js.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hat-mvo hat-mm hat-bleed"
     data-timeline="{{ '/assets/hatteras/data/timeline.json' | relative_url }}"
     data-places="{{ '/assets/hatteras/data/shoreline_rates.json' | relative_url }}"
     data-fill="{{ '/hatteras/management/nourishment/' | relative_url }}"
     data-road="{{ '/hatteras/management/nc-12/' | relative_url }}"
     data-groin="{{ '/hatteras/management/groins/' | relative_url }}">
  <div class="hat-shoremap-inner">
    <div class="hat-mm-key" aria-hidden="true">
      <span><i class="fill"></i>Beach nourishment</span>
      <span><i class="road"></i>NC-12 moved landward</span>
      <span><i class="bridge"></i>Bridge carrying NC-12</span>
      <span><i class="bridge open"></i>Bridge not in the model</span>
      <span><i class="groin"></i>Groins</span>
      <span><i class="storm"></i>Named storm</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hat-mm-chart" data-scroll-start="1"></div>
    <div class="hat-tl-tip" role="status" hidden></div>
    <p class="hat-caption hat-numbered">
      Where and when the island has been managed. Years run across; place along the island runs up, from Cape Point at the
      bottom to Oregon Inlet at the top, as on a map. Each mark covers the stretch of beach it affected: gold blocks are
      beach nourishment, orange bars are where NC-12 was moved landward, dark bands are bridges from the year they opened,
      and the red line is the Buxton groins, built in 1969. Blue triangles along the top are named storms that raised the
      water at the shore at least 3 m; the storm record starts in 1984. Hover over a mark for details, or click it to read more.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/js/management-map.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
